    <string name="rm_howto_tagline">Group your 13 cards into sequences and sets, then declare first.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_pill">2 to 6 players · two decks · table chips only</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_goal_title">Goal</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_goal_1">Arrange all 13 cards into valid groups and be the first to declare.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_goal_2">Everyone else loses points for the cards they couldn\'t group. The table goes on hand after hand until you leave.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_deal_title">The deal</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_deal_1">Two decks with two printed jokers. Everyone gets 13 cards.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_deal_2">One card is cut face up: every card of that rank is a joker too (a cut printed joker makes Aces jokers).</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_deal_3">One card starts the open pile; the rest form the closed pile.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_turn_title">Your turn</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_turn_1">Pick the top card of the closed pile or the open pile.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_turn_2">Then throw one card onto the open pile — or put it in the finish slot to declare.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_turn_3">Instead of picking you may DROP: 20 points before your first pick, 40 later.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_turn_4">Tap cards to select them. GROUP makes a new group; tap a group\'s bar to move the selected cards there. Grouping ON keeps your cards in their best groups.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_melds_title">Sequences and sets</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_melds_1">Pure sequence (1st life): 3+ cards of one suit in a row, no joker standing in. A-2-3 and Q-K-A both count; K-A-2 doesn\'t.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_melds_2">Impure sequence: the same with jokers filling gaps.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_melds_3">Set: 3 or 4 cards of one rank in different suits; jokers can fill in.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_melds_4">Jokers alone can sit in any group.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_declare_title">Declaring</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_declare_1">You need at least two sequences, one of them pure, and every card in a valid group.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_declare_2">When someone declares, everyone else arranges their cards and shows them within 30 seconds.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_declare_3">A wrong declaration costs 80 points and you sit out the rest of the hand.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_points_title">Points</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_points_1">A, K, Q, J = 10; number cards = their value; jokers = 0. The most you can lose is 80.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_points_2">No pure sequence: every card counts. A pure sequence but no second sequence: everything except it counts.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_points_3">With two sequences (one pure), only the cards outside valid groups count.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_points_4">Each point you lose costs chips; the winner collects them all.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_ex_1">5♥ 6♥ 7♥: a pure sequence — your 1st life.</string>
    <string name="rm_howto_ex_2">10♣ 10♠ 10♥: a set of three tens.</string>
